# Line-ending policy.
#
# Text files are stored with LF and checked out with LF on every OS, so a
# Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true no longer reports phantom "modified"
# files (the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning). Rust, TypeScript, JSON,
# YAML, and Markdown are all happy with LF on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts genuinely need CRLF (none today; kept for safety).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries (git detects these, but be explicit — the AVIF test
# fixtures in src-tauri/tests/fixtures must stay byte-exact).
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.gif   binary
